# Testing and Quality Assurance Rules

## Testing Best Practices

- Always use debugger statements for development and debugging
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test extension activation and deactivation
- Test all commands and their edge cases
- Use proper mocking for VSCode API calls

## Test Organization

- Create test files alongside source files
- Use descriptive test names
- Group related tests together
- Test both success and failure scenarios
- Mock external dependencies properly

## VSCode Extension Testing

- Test command registration and execution
- Test provider functionality
- Test activation events
- Test error handling scenarios
- Test user interaction flows

## Quality Assurance

- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Enable ESLint and Prettier
- Run tests before commits
- Check for memory leaks
  - Validate performance benchmarks

